---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="A guided iPhone scan, a 3D model of the patient's face, a plan shaped together and a recovery forecast up to month 12. How Rhinovate fits into a rhinoplasty consultation."
>
  <section class="page-head" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">One consultation, from the scan to the recovery forecast</h1>
      <p class="lead">Rhinovate fits into the consultation you already run. Here is what happens at each step, and what your patient sees.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="capture-title">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Step 1</p>
        <h2 id="capture-title">A guided scan on iPhone</h2>
        <p>The patient faces the front camera and turns through five positions: front, left, right, down and up. The app checks each angle in real time and captures automatically once the pose is right.</p>
        <dl class="specs">
          <div><dt>Device</dt><dd>iPhone with Face ID</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Capture</dt><dd>Five head positions, captured automatically</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-media">
        <div class="capture" role="group" aria-labelledby="capture-list-title">
          <p class="capture-head" id="capture-list-title"><span>Guided capture</span><span class="capture-state">5 of 5</span></p>
          <ol class="capture-list">
            {['Front', 'Left', 'Right', 'Down', 'Up'].map((pose) => (
              <li>
                <span>{pose}</span>
                <span class="capture-ok">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg>
                  Captured automatically
                </span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="model-title">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Step 2</p>
        <h2 id="model-title">A 3D model of the patient's face</h2>
        <p>An AI-assisted pipeline fits the scan to a 3D face model and places the facial landmarks. Each fit is checked against the raw depth data, and the nose is held to a tighter fit than the rest of the face.</p>
        <p>The model is ready while the patient is still in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="feature-media shot">
        <img src="/images/model-landmarks.webp" width="1200" height="960" alt="Demo face model at three quarters, with facial landmarks marked in blue" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Demo face, with landmarks marked</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="plan-title">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Step 3</p>
        <h2 id="plan-title">Plan the nose together</h2>
        <p>Shape the nose on the model with the patient beside you. Today and planned sit side by side, so the conversation stays on what the patient actually sees.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/">Try the plan view on the home page</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-media pair">
        <figure class="shot">
          <img src="/images/plan-today.webp" width="800" height="1000" alt="Demo face in profile with a dorsal hump and a low tip" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Today</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot">
          <img src="/images/plan-planned.webp" width="800" height="1000" alt="The same profile with a straight dorsum and a lifted tip, with today's profile dashed over it" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Planned, with today's profile dashed</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="prepare-title">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Step 4</p>
        <h2 id="prepare-title">Forecast the recovery</h2>
        <p>The forecast runs from the first days to month 12 on the planned nose. Swelling and bruising follow Rhinovate's healing model, calibrated on published clinical recovery data, zone by zone. It adjusts to the patient's skin thickness and age.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="/healing">Open the recovery forecast</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-media trio">
        <figure class="shot">
          <img src="/images/heal-day2.webp" width="800" height="1000" alt="Planned nose on day 2, swollen, with bruising around the eyes" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Day 2</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot">
          <img src="/images/heal-month1.webp" width="800" height="1000" alt="Planned nose at month 1, with mild swelling at the tip" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Month 1</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="shot">
          <img src="/images/heal-month12.webp" width="800" height="1000" alt="Planned nose at month 12, settled" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Month 12</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 id="limits-title">What a simulation is for</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Simulations are planning and communication aids. They show a plan and a typical recovery.</p>
        <p>They do not guarantee an outcome, and they do not replace the surgeon's judgment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
